// file (`template/study_lib.rs.in`). Edit the TEMPLATE, never a rendered copy: a rendered copy lives in a
// scratch directory under `std::env::temp_dir()` and is never committed.
//
// This file wraps a research STUDY file (owner's rule, 2026-11-15: a study is a FILE, built, loaded and
// sandboxed exactly like a strategy file). The study's folder is written VERBATIM to `src/study/`, and its
// entry file `<name>.rs` is this crate's module `study`: loaded by `#[path]`, it owns its folder, so a plain
// `mod matrix;` inside it resolves to its sibling `matrix.rs`, as it always has. Its entry is the contract
// `crates/vike-user-research/src/contract.rs` states:
//
//     pub fn run(ctx: &vike_user_research::StudyContext, params: &toml::Value)
//         -> Result<vike_user_research::StudyOutcome, vike_user_research::StudyError>
//
// and the coercion to `vike_user_research::StudyFn` below compile-checks that signature, naming the study.
//
// The exports cross BYTES only (`vike_rust_strategy::study`); what the bytes mean is
// `vike_user_research::file`'s, the one home of both halves. The handshake and the log slot are a strategy
// file's own exports, so one loader checks both kinds (`vike_rust_strategy::loader::load_study`). Every
// export catches a panic: none may unwind across the C ABI.
//
// ⚠ No crate-root `use` in this file, for the strategy template's reason: the study is a module of its
// own, and every name here is a fully-qualified path.

// ---- the study file, VERBATIM: `src/study/{{ENTRY_FILE}}` and its siblings ---------------------
#[path = "study/{{ENTRY_FILE}}"]
